OwnTV: stop ao_audiotrack spinning on an audio underrun.

While the AudioTrack is playing, ao_thread reads audio and writes it with a blocking write, which is
what paces the loop. When ao_read_data has nothing yet (an underrun: "Audio device underrun
detected"), it writes zero bytes, which returns at once, and the loop re-runs immediately with
p->lock held. The thread burns a whole core and the playloop, which needs p->lock to query the AO,
never gets it: mpv freezes on the first frame with no sound, for good.

Found on the TCL, 2026-10-07: catch-up (Stalker timeshift.php) froze at 0:01 in 5 of 8 opens,
both on core main and with the Phase A fixes. /proc showed `ao/audiotrack` in state R gaining
~140 ticks/s while mpv-cmd, demux and the decoder slept. Upstream master still has the loop
unchanged, so drop this patch only once ao_thread waits on a zero-sample read itself.

diff --git a/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c b/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
index f483ccc..c287337 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
@@ -584,6 +584,11 @@ static MP_THREAD_VOID ao_thread(void *arg)
             ts += MP_TIME_S_TO_NS(read_samples / (double)(ao->samplerate));
             ts += MP_TIME_S_TO_NS(AudioTrack_getLatency(ao));
             int samples = ao_read_data(ao, &p->chunk, read_samples, ts, NULL, false, false);
+            if (samples <= 0) {
+                // Nothing to play yet (underrun): wait instead of spinning with p->lock held.
+                mp_cond_timedwait(&p->wakeup, &p->lock, MP_TIME_MS_TO_NS(10));
+                continue;
+            }
             int ret = AudioTrack_write(ao, samples * ao->sstride);
             if (ret >= 0) {
                 p->written_frames += ret / ao->sstride;
